   129	      it the half-baked Lie superalgebra) in the same way as did V. Kac and R. Moody, see
   130	      § 3.1.1. For an arrow γ : v → v ′ in R the isomorphism h(γ) : h(v) → h(v ′ ) does not extend
   131	      to a homomorphism of the half-baked algebras. We define a root algebra supported on a
